## Why This Is Asked

Explores a practical, prefix-based data structure with duplicates, common in autocomplete and search features.

## Key Concepts

- Trie with per-node prefixCount and endCount
- Duplicate tracking via endCount
- Prefix-based queries in O(length(prefix))

## Code Example

```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.next = new Map();
    this.prefixCount = 0;
    this.endCount = 0;
  }
}
class Trie {
  constructor() { this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insert(word) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) node.next.set(ch, new TrieNode()); node = node.next.get(ch); node.prefixCount++; } node.endCount++; }
  erase(word) { if (!this.exists(word)) return false; let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { node = node.next.get(ch); node.prefixCount--; } node.endCount--; return true; }
  countWithPrefix(prefix) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of prefix) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) return 0; node = node.next.get(ch); } return node.prefixCount; }
  exists(word) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) return false; node = node.next.get(ch); } return node.endCount > 0; }
}
```

